    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0607" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.512 Boats/67</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Luther</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-08">June 8, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the German Ambassador and,
                    referring to His Excellency’s communication of March 12, 1934 and to previous
                    correspondence, regarding the imposition of a tax on the use of foreign built
                    boats by Section 761 (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) of the Revenue Act of
                    1932, has the honor to state that Section 613 of the Revenue Act of 1934,<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d402-f1"/> which has now become law, renders Section 761 (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) inapplicable after June 30, 1934.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
